      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://decodenyc.com/neighborhoods/ditmas-park"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The neighborhood is named after Abraham Ditmas, an early landowner who owned a large farm.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://ditmas-park.org/about"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Ditmas Park Historic District contains 2,000‑2,500 Victorian homes built between 1902 and 1914, many still standing.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ditmas_Park%2C_Brooklyn"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The area was first settled by Europeans in the mid‑17th century as part of Dutch New Netherland.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://ditmas-park.org/about"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Brooklyn Public Library’s Cortelyou branch sits at 1305 Cortelyou Road, a local landmark.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
